@attribute [Route("/components/" + nameof(HxAvatar))]
@attribute [Route("/components/" + nameof(HxAvatarStack))]

<ApiDoc Type="typeof(HxAvatar)">
    <MainContent>
        <p>Avatars are used to represent users or entities. They can display an image or initials as a fallback.</p>

        <DocHeading Title="Image" />
        <p>Use the <code>ImageSrc</code> parameter (with an optional <code>ImageAlt</code>) for image-based avatars.</p>
        <Demo Type="typeof(HxAvatar_Demo_Image)" Tabs="false" />

        <DocHeading Title="Initials" />
        <p>Use the child content for initials-based avatars. Combine with the <code>Color</code> parameter to apply a theme color.</p>
        <Demo Type="typeof(HxAvatar_Demo_Initials)" Tabs="false" />

        <DocHeading Title="Subtle" Level="4" />
        <p>Use <code>Subtle="true"</code> to create a subtle avatar.</p>
        <Demo Type="typeof(HxAvatar_Demo_Subtle)" Tabs="false" />

        <DocHeading Title="Sizes" />
        <p>Avatars come in multiple sizes: extra small, small, default, large, and extra large.</p>
        <Demo Type="typeof(HxAvatar_Demo_Sizes)" Tabs="false" />
        <p>Use a custom size by modifying the <code>--bs-avatar-size</code> CSS variable (e.g. <code>style="--bs-avatar-size: 8rem;"</code>), see <a href="#HxAvatar-css-variables">CSS variables</a>.</p>

        <DocHeading Title="Status indicator" />
        <p>
            Use the <code>Status</code> parameter to show a status indicator. Each status has a distinct shape and color.
            Because the status is conveyed purely through color and shape, the indicator renders with <code>role="img"</code>
            and an <code>aria-label</code> (customizable with the <code>StatusLabel</code> parameter) so assistive technologies can announce it.
        </p>
        <Demo Type="typeof(HxAvatar_Demo_Status)" Tabs="false" />

        <DocHeading Title="Status with sizes" Level="4" />
        <p>The status indicator scales with the avatar size.</p>
        <Demo Type="typeof(HxAvatar_Demo_StatusSizes)" Tabs="false" />

        <DocHeading Title="Customizing with CSS variables" />
        <p>
            The look of the avatar can be adjusted by overriding the CSS variables (see the <a href="#HxAvatar-css-variables">table below</a>)
            on the individual avatar (e.g. using the <code>style</code> attribute) or on any parent element.
        </p>
        <Demo Type="typeof(HxAvatar_Demo_CssVariables)" Tabs="false" />
    </MainContent>

    <CssVariables>
        <ApiDocCssVariable Name="--bs-avatar-size" Default="2.5rem">
            Width and height of the avatar (the font size of initials is derived from it). Overridden by the <code>Size</code> parameter classes.
        </ApiDocCssVariable>
        <ApiDocCssVariable Name="--bs-avatar-border-radius" Default="50%">
            Border radius of the avatar.
        </ApiDocCssVariable>
        <ApiDocCssVariable Name="--bs-avatar-border-width" Default="2px">
            Width of the border separating avatars in an <code>HxAvatarStack</code>.
        </ApiDocCssVariable>
        <ApiDocCssVariable Name="--bs-avatar-border-color" Default="var(--bs-bg-body)">
            Color of the border separating avatars in an <code>HxAvatarStack</code>.
        </ApiDocCssVariable>
        <ApiDocCssVariable Name="--bs-avatar-bg" Default="var(--bs-bg-2)">
            Background color of the avatar (when no <code>Color</code> is set).
        </ApiDocCssVariable>
        <ApiDocCssVariable Name="--bs-avatar-color" Default="var(--bs-fg-body)">
            Text color of the initials (when no <code>Color</code> is set).
        </ApiDocCssVariable>
        <ApiDocCssVariable Name="--bs-avatar-font-weight" Default="var(--bs-font-weight-medium)">
            Font weight of the initials (not set by default, the fallback applies).
        </ApiDocCssVariable>
        <ApiDocCssVariable Name="--bs-avatar-status-size" Default="0.75rem">
            Size of the status indicator. Overridden by the <code>Size</code> parameter classes.
        </ApiDocCssVariable>
        <ApiDocCssVariable Name="--bs-avatar-status-border-width" Default="2px">
            Border width of the status indicator.
        </ApiDocCssVariable>
        <ApiDocCssVariable Name="--bs-avatar-status-border-color" Default="var(--bs-bg-body)">
            Border color of the status indicator.
        </ApiDocCssVariable>
        <ApiDocCssVariable Name="--bs-avatar-stack-spacing" Default="-0.3">
            Overlap of the avatars in an <code>HxAvatarStack</code> (multiplier of the avatar size).
        </ApiDocCssVariable>
        <ApiDocCssVariable Name="--bs-avatar-stack-transition" Default="transform .2s ease-in-out">
            Transition of the avatars in an <code>HxAvatarStack</code> (on hover).
        </ApiDocCssVariable>
    </CssVariables>
</ApiDoc>

<ApiDoc Type="typeof(HxAvatarStack)">
    <p>Use <code>HxAvatarStack</code> to group multiple avatars together with an overlapping effect. Avatars are rendered in reverse order so the first avatar appears on top.</p>
    <Demo Type="typeof(HxAvatar_Demo_Stack)" Tabs="false" />

    <DocHeading Title="Stack with sizes" />
    <p>As a shorthand, use the <code>Size</code> parameter to set the size of all avatars in the stack.</p>
    <Demo Type="typeof(HxAvatar_Demo_StackSizes)" Tabs="false" />

    <DocHeading Title="Stack with count" />
    <p>Combine with initials to show a count of additional users.</p>
    <Demo Type="typeof(HxAvatar_Demo_StackCount)" Tabs="false" />
</ApiDoc>
